# Council runtime artifacts.
#
# COUNCIL_ROOT is derived from the script's own directory, so if the council is
# run from a CHECKOUT of this repo rather than from an install, every one of
# these lands INSIDE the repo. They are not incidental: a council log contains
# the full pitch -- the actual file contents under review, the diffs, and the
# user's directives. On the machine this was developed on, logs/ reached 1.1 GB
# across 7,224 fires covering real client work. NONE OF THIS MAY BE COMMITTED.
#
# NOTE ON FORMAT: git has NO inline comments. A `#` only opens a comment when it
# is the first character of the line; anywhere else it is a literal part of the
# pattern. An earlier version of this file put the descriptions to the RIGHT of
# each pattern, which silently disabled all three of them.
#
# consult_council.py -> logs/
council/logs/
# council_dialogue.py -> threads/ (full round-table threads)
council/threads/
# council_outcome.py -> labels + adjudications
council/outcomes.jsonl
# council_shadow_audit.py -> shadow-catch user rulings
council/shadow_outcomes.jsonl
# council_outcome.py -> drawn cohorts + their seeds
council/sample_cohorts.jsonl
# council_advisor.py -> auto-revert parks the REJECTED file content here.
# That is verbatim file content, so it is exactly as sensitive as logs/.
council/reverted/
# council_advisor.py -> payload probe, only written when DEBUG_PAYLOAD exists
council/payload_shape.jsonl
council/DEBUG_PAYLOAD
council/NO_AUTO_REVERT

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Runtime git-block stub dir (created by consult_council._ensure_nogit_stub)
council/_nogit/
council/DISABLED
# consult_council.py -> FAST depth switch (non-Claude members to low effort; GLOBAL, announced)
council/FAST
# consult_council.py -> layer-2 shadow-critic opt-in marker (needs this AND OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
council/SHADOW
# roster.json -> user-local roster override (who is on the council); per-install, like the markers
council/roster.json
# brain/ ships SCAFFOLDING only (schema, templates, validator). A VAULT is private
# content -- your facts, your paths, your commands -- and must never be committed
# here. The validator has NO default vault path -- it takes one as an argument --
# so `_brain/` below is a SUGGESTED name this ignore covers, not a convention the
# tooling knows about. Point the validator wherever your vault lives; it writes its
# attestation ledger inside that directory.
_brain/
**/.attestations.json

# docs/ -- only the rendered vector is version-controlled. The TikZ sources stay in the
# working tree but UNTRACKED, and a regenerated .pdf/.log/.aux is a diff on every rebuild
# for no reader's benefit. The one thing deliberately NOT ignored is what the README
# embeds: docs/*.svg, produced by `pdftocairo -svg`, which emits text as glyph paths and so
# carries no font dependency. The intermediate .png is not committed either.
docs/*.tex
docs/*.png
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.out
docs/*.fls
docs/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/*.synctex.gz
docs/*.toc
